&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SALEM,&amp;nbsp;Ore.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calibri,calibri_embeddedfont,calibri_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&mdash;&amp;nbsp;Oregon Housing and Community Services&amp;nbsp;(OHCS)&amp;nbsp;invests&amp;nbsp;$23.2 million&amp;nbsp;to stabilize&amp;nbsp;affordable&amp;nbsp;housing&amp;nbsp;properties&amp;nbsp;facing urgent financial challenges,&amp;nbsp;helping preserve&amp;nbsp;1,362&amp;nbsp;homes&amp;nbsp;at&amp;nbsp;rents people&amp;nbsp;can afford.&amp;nbsp;The Housing Stability Council&amp;nbsp;(HSC)&amp;nbsp;voted&amp;nbsp;Friday, Jan. 9&amp;nbsp;to approve the funding for 15 properties&amp;nbsp;located&amp;nbsp;in Multnomah County.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calibri,calibri_embeddedfont,calibri_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
